---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms on which you may use the AIB Robot website and submit an order request for an adult companion figure or the expression-head figure."
  requireAge={false}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of use and sale.</h1>
      <p class="lead">These terms govern your use of this website and any order request you submit. They should be read with our privacy, returns, shipping, and compliance pages.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose" style="padding-bottom:4.5rem">
      <p class="fine">Last updated 15 November 2026.</p>

      <h2>The site</h2>
      <p>
        AI Bionic Robot (AIB Robot) sells adult companion figures and one adult expression-head figure through this English-language website. Nothing on this site is an offer to sell until we confirm a specific unit, a final price, and a shipping arrangement in writing. Companion figures are transitional products in a catalog whose longer subject is AI bionic robots.
      </p>

      <h2>Adults only</h2>
      <p>
        You must be 18 or older to enter and to submit an inquiry. You confirm that viewing and purchasing these products is lawful where you live and where a package would be received. We may refuse a request that we believe is unlawful, or that we cannot fulfill honestly.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices, stock, and descriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Public prices are the figures shown on each product page: STPE companions at $2,199 beside a previous list price of $2,599 as of 15 November 2026, silicone companions at 4 October 2025 suggested retail, and the expression-head figure at $3,099 as of 15 November 2026. Warehouse availability is taken from the November 2026 US and EU lists. Measurements are taken from the notes named on each product page; where a figure is missing, it is omitted. We may correct errors. A request in your inquiry bag is not a reserved unit. A contract is formed only when we accept a confirmed order in writing, after inventory and the final price have been agreed.
      </p>

      <h2>Order requests and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Checkout on this site is an order request. We do not take card payments on these pages. If we can fulfill the request, we will confirm the details and arrange payment through a high-risk processor once one is approved. Until then, no charge is made. You agree not to send card numbers by email.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of the site</h2>
      <p>
        You may not misuse this site, attempt to interfere with it, scrape it aggressively, or use it to send unlawful or abusive messages. The design, text, and arrangement of this site are ours. Photographs remain subject to their original rights. Where a photograph carries a printed overlay, the specification table on the product page is the listing, and we do not alter the photograph to remove that overlay.
      </p>

      <h2>AI products</h2>
      <p>
        Statements about the expression-head figure and the AI voice box are limited to the notes described on those pages. We do not promise that an expression head already works on US or EU home Wi-Fi, and we do not claim that it walks or moves on its own. Those limits are part of the product description.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        We are responsible for fulfilling an accepted order with reasonable care, and for the remedies described on the returns page if a product arrives damaged or with a factory defect. We are not responsible for a lawful customs seizure in a destination you chose, for a delay a carrier or a warehouse causes after we have handed the goods over, or for loss that could not reasonably have been foreseen. Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud, or any liability that cannot be limited by law. Where liability can be limited, it is limited to the amount you paid for the order in question.
      </p>

      <h2>Law</h2>
      <p>
        If a dispute arises, we would rather resolve it directly. The law that applies, and the courts that have jurisdiction, will be stated in the written confirmation of an accepted order — we will not invent a governing-law clause tied to a country of incorporation we have not published. Until then, mandatory consumer protections in your country of residence, where they apply, are not displaced by this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
